      "bufferPaths": "0.5 acre — access paths between zones"
    },
    "honestTerrain": "It's hilly. Not flat farmland. You'll need to terrace parts of the garden. The good news: terracing is traditional in Kumaon, locals know how, and terraced gardens actually drain better than flat ones.",
    "soil": "Kumaon soil is rocky but fertile. Amend heavily with cow dung compost (you'll have plenty). Rocky bits can be cleared and used for walls/terracing.",
    "waterSource": "Borewell (200-400ft) + Kosi river nearby + monsoon rain collection"
  },

